#uuid "cb8b0f6c-4a71-5c9b-bc62-54e3ad24cf0e" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426815 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426821 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426822 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426826 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426831 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1077 "selection" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426821 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426836 1079 #uuid "cd4aac9d-4227-5875-926d-41c64f7175cf" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426817 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426819 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426820 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426823 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426828 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1077 "selection" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426819 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426837 1079 #uuid "ef163c6e-9635-5101-b558-ea7a832bcdd4" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426837 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1069 "q-171040" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1071 "Simplify the following sentence: \"$y$ is irrational and it is an irrational number, or $y$ is irrational or it is a negative number.\"" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1072 #uuid "0d9b6544-a3d6-5482-a66b-0b543948f593" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426838 1074 "First, we simplify the phrase \"$y$ is irrational and it is an irrational number\" to just \"$y$ is irrational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is irrational, or $y$ is irrational or it is a negative number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$y$ is irrational or $y$ is irrational, or it is a negative number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$y$ is irrational or $y$ is irrational\" to just \"$y$ is irrational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is irrational, or it is a negative number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$y$ is irrational or negative.\"" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426835 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1069 "q-170742" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1071 "$n$ is less than $10$ **or** $13$, **and** $n$ is an integer\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $X(n):$ $n$ is less than $10$\n\n- $Y(n):$ $n$ is less than $13$\n\n- $Z(n):$ $n$ is an integer" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1072 #uuid "17d0f2d8-abc7-53ff-a964-9b193b159c69" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426839 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:  \n\n- **Part 1:** $n$ is less than $10$ or $13.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is less than }10}_{⏟}}_{X}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{n\\text{ is less than }13}_{⏟}}_{Y},\n$$\n\nthat is, $X∨Y.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $n$ is an integer. This corresponds to $Z.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is less than }10\\text{ or }13}_{⏟}}_{X∨Y}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{n\\text{ is an integer}}_{⏟}}_{Z},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(X∨Y)∧Z.$" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426834 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1069 "q-175552" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1071 "Find the truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the set of positive integers:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd\n\n- $Q(x):$ $12$ is divisible by $x$" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1072 #uuid "82d493f7-be8a-5b02-922e-c52bcfe9d8a4" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426840 1074 "The truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∧Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$ \n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of all positive odd integers, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∧Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}\\cap \\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426836 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1069 "q-177759" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1071 "Simplify the following sentence: \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1072 #uuid "be776820-4de7-562d-ad85-1f2cc185142d" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true] [17592186426841 1074 "First, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$z$ is rational or positive.\"" 13194139534591 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-19fe9774-58ed-565f-9cbb-223d3c49f77e" 17592186426814 "answer-46192eea-f4ae-5745-ab2b-1935f29c22a2" 17592186426815 "answer-46ea5f59-2e7f-5295-8695-9592bd42ab82" 17592186426816 "answer-5350a4a4-f298-59d8-9612-4c7517461dce" 17592186426817 "answer-550263d1-e585-5aa0-8873-ca1a37d6d639" 17592186426818 "answer-7d17b8f6-c501-5b6a-9f25-24fb0da0b825" 17592186426819 "answer-8724cd76-5bf1-5bcc-bde0-4e58af383bf0" 17592186426820 "answer-9046c2c1-c0ee-5e13-92fe-5436918ed8ee" 17592186426821 "answer-91799f63-a171-5d71-abd6-d2ac6eb622bc" 17592186426822 "answer-97073a41-e9c9-5ba0-a4bd-c3da3d9761ba" 17592186426823 "answer-975840e4-95b6-570a-bca6-50be4fce0c45" 17592186426824 "answer-9b251db1-3373-5f6f-983a-96f7fe8666bd" 17592186426825 "answer-a892fa0b-ae64-5844-bb4e-4a9d0eb3ece7" 17592186426826 "answer-a9428b0b-b88e-5b0f-a9db-05a9a71468a8" 17592186426827 "answer-ae7c50ca-e9d1-5f38-8f63-d041811dcbb9" 17592186426828 "answer-b35083dd-72dd-533d-9726-6630eec2aaae" 17592186426829 "answer-bda4b648-d128-5a9f-af66-b574da891c6b" 17592186426830 "answer-c455468d-3494-592f-8fea-f7eb970fc2bd" 17592186426831 "answer-c69e7e45-595b-57f9-9f1e-7da09afbdb28" 17592186426832 "answer-f8d36d58-81e3-5ce6-a949-0b1fb3544fff" 17592186426833 "answer-field-6b76c296-5c89-50a5-b725-0525be121d8e" 17592186426834 "answer-field-cb8b0f6c-4a71-5c9b-bc62-54e3ad24cf0e" 17592186426835 "answer-field-cd4aac9d-4227-5875-926d-41c64f7175cf" 17592186426836 "answer-field-ef163c6e-9635-5101-b558-ea7a832bcdd4" 17592186426837 "question-0d9b6544-a3d6-5482-a66b-0b543948f593" 1